# The Brindle 3D workshop's scenes, copied into this project with their paths
# repointed by tools/vendor_workshop.gd (MIGRATION_3D §6, M2b). Generated from
# prototypes/brindle_3d/, which is the committed original; run the tool after
# cloning and after each delivery of his. Never edited here, never committed.
view3d/workshop/

# The approved asset pack (SPECS §13): what the game uses is committed.
#
# The PNGs are only 4 MB and they *define* the locked palette in
# content/palette.txt, so the repo has to carry them — a clone without them
# cannot run the asset tests.
#
# **The audio is committed too, as of 2026-09-13.** It was excluded on the
# grounds that "nothing references them, while §14 Audio is still TBD", and both
# halves of that stopped being true the night §14 was settled and view/sound.gd
# was written. A clone without it is a silent game with three failing tests, and
# a test that only passes on the machine the files happen to be on is worse than
# no test. 97 MB, which takes .git from 5 MB to about 100 — cheap against a
# clone that does not work.
#
# Still excluded: 5 MB of animated GIF previews, which Godot does not import at
# all (no .import file is generated for a single one of them), and which nothing
# will ever reference. Re-downloadable from the itch.io URL recorded in
# assets/NinjaAdventure/LICENCE-as-downloaded.md.
assets/**/*.gif
